<title>USA: TABLE-Keystone Consolidated Q2 shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Keystone Consolidated Q2 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS, Texas 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months	  Six Months</p>
<p>				     Ended June 30,     Ended June 30,</p>
<p>				    1997	1996	1997	1996</p>
<p>Net sales		   $103,232  $90,655  $192,381   $170,118</p>
<p>Gross profit		 $13,431   $7,367   $21,789    $12,443</p>
<p>Net income (loss)	  $4,347     $810    $5,971	$(327)</p>
<p>Primary net income (loss) per</p>
<p>common share		  $0.46    $0.14     $0.63     $(0.06)</p>
<p>Fully diluted net income</p>
<p>(loss) per common share   $0.45    $0.14     $0.62     $(0.06)</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>and common equivalent</p>
<p>shares -- primary	    9,295    5,693     9,279	5,678</p>
<p>		 (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Increased revenues were attributed in part to higher selling prices and elevated production rates.</p>
<p>Keystone plans to invest $75 million through 1999 in capital projects aimed at improving efficiency.</p>
</text>
